        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fig and honey tart has a ricotta and honey filling that bakes to a dense, creamy set in a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blind-baking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "blind-baked"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " shortcrust case. Sliced figs are pressed into the filling before baking; they sink slightly as the custard sets. The filling takes less than 5 minutes to make. The key variable is the figs: ripe figs become soft and jammy; underripe ones stay leathery."
          }
        ]
